    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n6863" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀνακῶς</span></b> , Adv.
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>carefully,</i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀνακῶς ἔχειν τινός</span> look
				<i>well</i> to a thing, give <i>good heed</i> to it, <i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				1.24
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				8.109
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Th.
				8.102
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				<u>Thes.</u>
				33
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀ. θεραπεύειν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hp.
					<u>Carn.</u>
					19
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὰς </span>(<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τῆς</span> Pierson) 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θύρας ἀ. ἔχων</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pl.Com.
					202
				</span></i>
			.— 
				Dor.
			 acc. to <i><span class="en">
				Erot.
			</span></i> s. v., but found in 
				Ion.
			 and Early 
				Att.
			 (Connected with <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄναξ</span> by <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
			</span></i> l. c., cf. <i><span class="en">
				<u>AB</u>
				391
			</span></i>, Phot.<i><span class="en">
				p.113R.
			</span></i>)</div>
